ant one you still have it but it's  when you really want it as opposed to oh  I saw that cookie I'm gonna eat that  cookie and that's what you helped with  the Obamas when when you first met  Michelle Obama you helped clean out  their pantry yep and it makes a huge  difference because now the kids are  running through the you know the kitchen  and instead of grabbing you know bag of  chips they're grabbing some grapes  because they're just getting what's  around them and I can attest John is in  the market too because he talks about it  every morning that's right  you've made this movie a New York dude  you make house call you talk about kids  and the influence we mentioned that you  had in school systems in the country  about making food healthier we've seen  the Trump administration turned that  around really and say that it's either  too costly and that a lot of these  healthier foods are actually being  thrown away if you could do anything now  to change maybe the initial plan you had  what would that be well I think it's  first important to note that the vast  majority of what we did around nutrition  and health and schools is still intact  there's a little tweaking around the  edges but the majority of what we  accomplished this is there because the  fact of the matter is moms and families  and parents they want good food for  their kids in schools I think the  program needs more money one of the  things you know first and foremost one  of the things that's most inserting  right now is proposals from the GOP to  roll back snap school nutrition  assistance program kicking millions of  vulnerable Americans off of off of food  stamps so like that's that's very  concerning but we need to invest in our  kids well-being it's the foundation of a  thriving economy it's the foundation of  a thriving health care system and if we  don't we're gonna see costs continue to  skyrocket in the decades to come and  you're a new father how has that helped  change how you look at