e're  supposed to do but what I try to do a  lot in this book is focused on the how  the vast majority of Americans are  trying to eat better but they're failing  and they're feeling because we don't  actually give strategies and to  implement these changes in our daily  lives and so everybody ends up falling  short and then just sort of throwing  their hands up and giving up but if we  make these kind of steps not only can we  transform our own health but have a huge  impact on the environment I mean food  and agriculture is the number two driver  of climate change of greenhouse gas  emissions it's the number one cause of  preventable death and disease so we can  solve some of these fundamental problems  into what we're eating every day have a  huge impact on so many the challenges  that we're facing not many people have  an impact on the president and the first  family the way you have you write in the  book that the Secret Service got used to  you running through the White House  because you had to have dinner on the  table by 6:30 yeah what was it like I  mean now looking back you've had a few  years to reflect on working with the  first family and feeding them literally  yeah well it was first the greatest  honor of my life and I think we'll  always be it was intense and you know  because of all the policy work and let's  move working for the first lady  you know dinner was like I felt often  like a sort of a single parent like oh  my god I gotta get to dinner on the  table got 30 minutes but the thing that  struck me most was that no matter where  he was or where she was they  dinner's a family unless he was overseas  or in California they ate as a family  every night and he left everything that  he was dealing with at the door okay  same casts we're gonna have to go eat a  little better goes on sale tomorrow
 

